[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **The C library has no error surface.** `max_size_frame` is a total function: it
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m takes three `uint32_t` by value, performs only unsigned arithmetic, and returns
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m unconditionally. There is no rejection path, no sentinel return, no error code,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m no assertion, no range check, and no null check to replicate — there are no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m pointer parameters to null-check and no enum parameters to feed an out-of-range
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m variant.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Consequently the *classical* error-surface table has zero rows:
