[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    16[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Axes the C actually branches on
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    17[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    18[0m:[38;5;10m[49m There is no runtime option struct, no mode/flag setter, no `#ifdef`, and no
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    19[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `if`/`switch` — the header exposes one entry point and it is also the lowest-level
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    20[0m:[38;5;10m[49m entry point, so "convenience wrapper vs low-level API" does not apply. The
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    21[0m:[38;5;10m[49m branching is entirely *value*-driven, through three relational sub-expressions
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    22[0m:[38;5;10m[49m used as 0/1 multipliers:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    23[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | axis | source of the branch | distinct states |
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m |---|---|---|
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m | A. stereo flag | `(channels == 2)` / `(channels != 2)` | `channels == 2`, `channels != 2` |
